        "id": "p30-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\left(2\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac35\\right)\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{24}{25}$",
          "worked": "Let $A=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac35\\right)$, so $\\cos A=\\frac35$.\n\nUsing $\\sin(2A)=2\\sin A\\cos A$.\n\nFrom a right triangle, $\\sin A=\\frac45$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(2\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac35\\right)\\right)&=2\\left(\\frac45\\right)\\left(\\frac35\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{24}{25}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\left(2\\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt3)\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
          "worked": "Let $A=\\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt3)$, so $\\tan A=\\sqrt3$.\n\nThis means $A=\\frac\\pi3$, so $\\sin A=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$ and $\\cos A=\\frac12$.\n\nUsing $\\sin(2A)=2\\sin A\\cos A$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(2\\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt3)\\right)&=2\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
